From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tatsuki Tanaka <tatsuki@tanakatatsuki.dev>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:32:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: fix current sign on SM8475
 firmware

The SM8475 (cape) battery firmware reports CURRENT_NOW as negative while
charging (verified on xiaomi-marble: -800 mA on a wall charger while
voltage, capacity and charge counter rise). The power supply ABI wants
positive when charging, so UPower showed the battery as discharging.

---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 7b35d16148..b7464deafa 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1450,6 +1450,9 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_sm8350_callback(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
 			break;
 		case BATT_CURR_NOW:
 			battmgr->status.current_now = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
+			/* This firmware reports charging current as negative */
+			if (battmgr->bat_const_curr_id)
+				battmgr->status.current_now = -battmgr->status.current_now;
 			break;
 		case BATT_TEMP:
 			val = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
